12. ALLOCATION OF CONTRIBUTIONS, INCOME AND EXPENSES
12.1 Unless otherwise permitted by Superannuation Law, the Trustee must
allocate amounts which are directly attributable to a Member to that
person's Member Account (or between the various Member Accounts
maintained for the Member at the discretion of the Trustee) within the
timeframe required by Superannuation Law or at such other times as
the Trustee determines, including:
(a) contributions;
(b) transfers;
(c) insurance premiums;

